! STAGE B: r1's CURRENT startup-file shape, on a throwaway node.
!
! @@HASH@@ is replaced at run time by a type-9 hash generated ON the probe
! (step B2). No fleet hash is copied here, and this file is never committed
! with a real value in it.
!
! The plaintext behind that hash is the one in step B2's PLAIN variable, so
! after boot we can test all three possibilities:
!   - admin accepts vrnetlab's 'admin'      -> the secret line was REFUSED
!   - admin accepts the secret's plaintext  -> the secret line APPLIED
!   - admin accepts neither                 -> worse than predicted
!
hostname bp-c8k-b
!
no aaa new-model
!
username admin privilege 15 secret 9 @@HASH@@
!
ip domain name rcn.lab
!
line vty 0 4
 logging synchronous
 login local
 transport input all
!
end
